e);\n81-   2. other gaps;\n82-   3. needs_evidence, grouped by Lead role;\n83-   4. na_candidates;\n84-   5. likely_pass;\n85-   6. injection attempts;\n86-   7. the scope and its limits: the model used, how many likely_pass items survived the challenge, how many gaps the hunt found, and whether `--conservative` was used.\n87-\n88-   Keep sentences short and plain, and give `path:line` for every claim.\n89-10. **Offer next steps.** The `brace-record` skill can turn findings into draft record entries. The `brace-tests` skill can write tests for needs_evidence items.\n90-\n91-## Findings format\n92-\n93-```json\n94-{\n95-  \"brace_checklist\": \"2026-10-01\",\n96-  \"repo\": \"owner/name or path\",\n97-  \"commit\": \"git commit hash, or null\",\n98-  \"reviewed_at\": \"ISO 8601 time\",\nusage: validate_findings.py [-h] [--repo REPO] [--fix] [--conservative] [--aspect {B,R,A,C,E}] [--batch BATCH] [--before-challenges] findings\n\nCheck a brace-findings.json file and, optionally, fix ratings the rules decide.\n\nUsage:\n  python validate_findings.py FINDINGS.json [--repo DIR] [--fix] [--conservative] [--aspect B|R|A|C|E]\n\n  --repo DIR       The reviewed codebase, used to confirm quotes. Default: the folder\n                   that holds FINDINGS.json.\n  --fix            Apply the rating rules: a \"no\" answer or a red flag makes a gap; a\n                   likely_pass that breaks a rule is lowered; a \"yes\" backed only by\n                   docs, or by a quote not found in the code, becomes \"unknown\". Never\n                   raises a rating. Writes the file back, then validates.\n  --conservative   Also turn every likely_pass into needs_evidence. Use with small\n                   models: the review then only finds gaps and can't suggest a pass.\n  --aspect X       Check only one aspect's items (for files made with new_findings.py --aspect).\n\nExit 0 if valid, 1 if not, 2 on bad usage.\n\npositional arguments:","stderr":"","interrupted":false,"isImage":false